{#-
  PyTest Creator — standardized ART test-script SKELETON.

  This is NOT a prompt. It renders a complete, runnable, conformant Allied Telesis
  `framework` (ATTestSet/ATTestCase) script from a reviewed sequence. The LLM fills
  the FREE SLOTS only (marked  # >>> FILL ... <<<  ); the frame — header, TestSet
  structure, per-step TestCase classes, the logging contract inside each main(), and
  the __main__ footer — is fixed so output is standardized and mechanically checkable.

  Three slot kinds (never conflated — see LOGGING-CONTRACT.md + PLAN §1.4):
    1. TestSet.configure()/tear_down()  = suite setup/cleanup, config commands, NO pass/fail
    2. TestCase_<n>.main()              = ONE verification step; logging contract APPLIES
    3. framework automatics             = nothing here (subclassing gets them free)

  RULE FOR EDITORS (learned the hard way, 2026-07-28): a comment in this file ships into
  every generated script, and where prose and EXAMPLE disagree the model copies the
  EXAMPLE. Four separate defects in generated scripts came from wrong examples here or in
  the prompt (`port = 'port1.0.1'`, `split()[-2:] == [...]`, `self.dut.portA` in init).
  So: guidance for the MODEL belongs in pt_generate_script.jinja rules; this file carries
  only what a reader of the finished test needs, and every example here must be correct
  against the real corpus. `tests/test_prompt_examples.py` enforces that.

  Idioms below are grounded in the 830-script corpus (counts as of 2026-07-28):
    mode(')#') = config mode 4812 | mode('#') = priv exec 4253 | mode(']#') = stack 382
    cmd('conf t') is NOT the idiom (69)   |   port.name for CLI text 1013 (vs 241 bare); literals 350
    FEATURES=['ALL'] 291/306   |   init_swi('swi_a') 621/~650   |   init_stk('stk_a') 191/191

  Context expected:
    case_key       e.g. "AWPTCM-T33234"
    case_title     one-line title
    objective_lines wrapped comment lines of the refined objective (the "expected results"
                   this script must demonstrate) — carried into the .py so the declarative
                   context is never lost between the sequence and the fill. May be empty.
    extra_imports  list of extra `from framework...`/module import lines (may be empty)
    setup_steps    list of {action} suite-setup actions -> TestSet.configure() (may be empty)
    steps          list of {n, action, verify, kind} verification steps -> TestCase_<n>
    switches       list of switch VARIABLE names to bind (e.g. ["dut","lp"]) — default ["swi_a"]
    setup_keys     the .setup [switch] KEYS those variables look up, positionally
                   (swi_a/swi_b/...); see _setup_keys_for(). Falls back to the variable name.
    stacks         list of stack names to bind (e.g. ["stk_a"]) — may be empty
    needs_portlink truthy if the case uses port links (renders an init_portlink FILL slot)
-#}
